      "takeoffDescription": "",
      "comments": "This site is about 1 hour NorthEast from Yerevan. During the summer, a very consistent sea breeze from Lake Sevan provides dynamic ridge soaring. A grassy launch is approached via a 20 walk. A popular site for new pilots as well as experienced pilots as lots of airtime can be had without lots of work. Thermal flying is possible but I personally have not climbed more than 300 meters above launch. Watch out for over developing clouds capable of cloud suck. Many landings in the large LZ require the use of big ears or spiral dives to get down."
    },
